   "source": [
    "# 1. Beispieldaten erzeugen"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "f5bb0f5a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from scipy import stats"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "4d0fd7da",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "<class 'pandas.DataFrame'>\n",
      "<class 'pandas.Series'>\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"aktie_a\": [0.02, 0.01, -0.01, 0.03],\n",
    "    \"aktie_b\": [0.01, -0.02, 0.02, 0.04],\n",
    "    \"aktie_c\": [0.05, -0.02, 0.02, 0.04]\n",
    "})\n",
    "print(type(df))\n",
    "print(type(df[\"aktie_a\"]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "34892ed4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2. \"pandas.Series\" UND \"pandas.Dataframe\" INS \"numpy.ndarray\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fede800a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Objektyp <class 'numpy.ndarray'>\n",
      "Objektyp <class 'numpy.ndarray'>\n",
      "1-D-Array:\n",
      " [ 0.02  0.01 -0.01  0.03]\n",
      "----\n",
      "2-D-Array:\n",
      " [[ 0.02  0.01  0.05]\n",
      " [ 0.01 -0.02 -0.02]\n",
      " [-0.01  0.02  0.02]\n",
      " [ 0.03  0.04  0.04]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "werte = df[\"aktie_a\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "renditen = df[[\"aktie_a\", \"aktie_b\", \"aktie_c\"]].to_numpy()\n",
    "print(\"Objektyp\",type(werte))\n",
    "print(\"Objektyp\",type(renditen))\n",
    "print(\"1-D-Array:\\n\", werte)\n",
    "print(\"----\")\n",
    "print(\"2-D-Array:\\n\", renditen)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d94974d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. NumPy-Kovarianzmatrix aus einem pandas.DataFrame und/oder numpy.2array"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4fc6add",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- np.cov() betrachtet standardmäßig jede Zeile als Variable. Bei deinem DataFrame (bzw. in daraus erzeugte np matrix (numpy.2array)s. oben) befinden sich die Variablen in den Spalten."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "de2dae9c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[0.00029167 0.000125   0.000225  ]\n",
      " [0.000125   0.000625   0.00059167]\n",
      " [0.000225   0.00059167 0.00095833]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "kovarianzmatrix = np.cov(renditen, rowvar=False, ddof=1)\n",
    "# ddof=1 bedeutet: Wir verwenden die Stichprobenkovarianz, nicht die Populationskovarianz.\n",
    "print(kovarianzmatrix)\n",
    "# rowvar=False bedeutet: Die Variablen beziehungsweise Aktien stehen in den Spalten. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f48c8a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Einfacher mit pandas: Für einen normalen DataFrame ist häufig diese Variante verständlicher:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "c0368be8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "kovarianzmatrix = df[\n",
    "    [\"aktie_a\", \"aktie_b\", \"aktie_c\"]\n",
    "].cov()\n",
    "#Vorteil: Das Ergebnis ist wieder ein DataFrame mit Beschriftungen:\n",
    "# Für Matrixrechnungen und Optimierung: kovarianz_array = kovarianz_df.to_numpy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6cb6e731",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4. NumPy-Ergebnis wieder in pandas umwandeln"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "78110c89",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## A. Eindimensionales Array zu Series"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "ee7a550b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "array = np.array([0.02, 0.01, -0.01, 0.03])\n",
    "\n",
    "serie = pd.Series(array, name=\"aktie_a\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "825ded2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "serie = pd.Series(\n",
    "    array,\n",
    "    index=df.index,\n",
    "    name=\"aktie_a\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "12e9314f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## B. Zweidimensionales Array zu DataFrame"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "3280727d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "   aktie_a  aktie_b\n",
      "0     0.02     0.01\n",
      "1     0.01    -0.02\n",
      "2    -0.01     0.02\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "array = np.array([\n",
    "[0.02, 0.01],\n",
    "[0.01, -0.02],\n",
    "[-0.01, 0.02]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "neuer_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "array,\n",
    "columns=[\"aktie_a\", \"aktie_b\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(neuer_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "405fc692",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "   aktie_a  aktie_b\n",
      "0     0.02     0.01\n",
      "1     0.01    -0.02\n",
      "2    -0.01     0.02\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "neuer_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    array,\n",
    "    index=df.index[:3],\n",
    "    # index aus dem Original-DataFrame übernehmen\n",
    "    columns=[\"aktie_a\", \"aktie_b\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(neuer_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "3fb4d9ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "spalten = [\"aktie_a\", \"aktie_b\", \"aktie_c\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "kovarianz_array = np.cov(\n",
    "    df[spalten].to_numpy(),\n",
    "    rowvar=False,\n",
    "    ddof=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "kovarianz_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    kovarianz_array,\n",
    "    index=spalten,\n",
    "    columns=spalten\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "89a8379e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 5. Probleme und Herausforderungen"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "686db307",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## A. Fehlende Werte"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "819cf03e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Angenommen, eine Spalte enthält NaN:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Python\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "\"aktie_a\": [0.02, 0.01, np.nan, 0.03],\n",
    "\"aktie_b\": [0.01, np.nan, 0.02, 0.04]\n",
    "})\n",
    "```\n",
    "-  Diese SciPy-Berechnung kann dann ein ungültiges Ergebnis liefern:\n",
    "\n",
    "Python\n",
    "stats.pearsonr(df[\"aktie_a\"], df[\"aktie_b\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "- Falsch: Spalten getrennt bereinigen\n",
    "```Python\n",
    "a = df[\"aktie_a\"].dropna()\n",
    "b = df[\"aktie_b\"].dropna()\n",
    "```\n",
    "- Das kann problematisch sein, weil danach Renditen aus unterschiedlichen Zeitpunkten miteinander verglichen werden."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "ea3c3bca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Richtig: gemeinsame Zeilen auswählen\n",
    "daten = df[[\"aktie_a\", \"aktie_b\"]].dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "korrelation, p_wert = stats.pearsonr(\n",
    "    daten[\"aktie_a\"].to_numpy(),\n",
    "    daten[\"aktie_b\"].to_numpy()\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "41e11b40",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Alternative mit nan_policy\n",
    "\n",
    "-   Einige SciPy-Funktionen unterstützen:\n",
    "\n",
    "    ```Python\n",
    "    stats.ttest_ind(\n",
    "    df[\"aktie_a\"],\n",
    "    df[\"aktie_b\"],\n",
    "    nan_policy=\"omit\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    ```\n",
    "\n",
    "- Aber nicht jede SciPy-Funktion besitzt denselben Umgang mit fehlenden Werten. Gemeinsames dropna() ist bei zusammengehörigen Finanzzeitreihen meist transparenter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6aabb432",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## B. Unterschiedliche Längen"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0bfa8c41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Das geht nicht:\n",
    "\n",
    "    ```Python\n",
    "    a = np.array([1, 2, 3])\n",
    "    b = np.array([1, 2])\n",
    "    stats.pearsonr(a, b)\n",
    "    ```\n",
    "- Beide Variablen müssen gleich viele zusammengehörige Beobachtungen haben."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "60ffa06c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## C. Zweidimensional statt eindimensional"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2aabe18",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Das hier ist ein DataFrame:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Python\n",
    "df[[\"aktie_a\"]]\n",
    "```\n",
    "- Es besitzt die Form:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Plain Text\n",
    "(4, 1)\n",
    "```\n",
    "- Das hier ist eine Series:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Python\n",
    "df[\"aktie_a\"]\n",
    "```\n",
    "- Sie besitzt die Form:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Plain Text\n",
    "(4,)\n",
    "```\n",
    "- Viele statistische Funktionen erwarten für eine einzelne Variable (4,), also eindimensionale Daten.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Umwandlung:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Python\n",
    "werte = df[[\"aktie_a\"]].to_numpy().ravel()\n",
    "```\n",
    "- Einfacher:\n",
    "\n",
    "```Python\n",
    "werte = df[\"aktie_a\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1da6d98f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## D. Indexverlust"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d93fe5f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Nach:"
   ]
  },
  {
